{"seq":15,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:31:19.677Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"789127c11596c4e71256f99707aee800461b139bea93f89ff33e6de0419693d4","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"Bettina, here's what I found in #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests (cheat sheet, 2025-10-05, 2025-11-02, 2026-05-18):\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)\n- Ticket #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open per Moss's cheat sheet.\n- Ticket PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (Gate 4B). This is from your Dec 2025 cutover recap, not Moss's notes, and it was during the cutover, so check whether it's still live.\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by their warehouse managers (cheat sheet).\n- Ticket #4419 (see conflict below): barge slip 7 schedule sync, plus a request for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift (Moss's 11/2/2025 digest).\n- No ticket number given: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering supplied a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher (cheat sheet).\n\nConflict to resolve before the review: Moss's cheat sheet puts #4419 on PHL (Yard_Dwell_Summary), but the 11/2/2025 digest puts #4419 on Driftmoor (slip 7 sync). One of them is probably a typo, and I can't tell which from the notes. Kwame can confirm.\n\nLeft out: Pellow Home Living (PD-4821, #8812) and Saltmarsh (PD-4824, PD-4827), as they're other accounts.\n\nI found no other PHL or Driftmoor tickets in the Coastal channels. I couldn't see ticket-system data or any account folders, only what's written in those channels and notes.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
